Represents a specific sellable, stockable, or consumable variant of a product (the actual item tracked in inventory, sales, and purchases).
Key Functional Use Cases:

Individual items with specific attributes (color, size, capacity, etc.)
Inventory tracking (on hand, available, reserved, forecasted)
Sales, purchases, and POS transactions
Manufacturing (as component or finished good)
Pricing per variant, barcode, and internal reference
Multi-company, multi-warehouse stock levels
Product listings on website and in reports

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
product_tmpl_id → product.template (required, parent)
name (inherited + variant name), default_code (SKU), barcode
lst_price (public price), standard_price (cost)
uom_id, uom_po_id
available_in_pos, sale_ok, purchase_ok, active
attribute_value_ids → Many2many to product.attribute.value
Computed: price, qty_available, virtual_available, incoming_qty, outgoing_qty

Critical Hooks: onchange_product_tmpl_id, _compute_quantities, _get_name, variant creation logic
Security: product.group_product_manager + company + warehouse rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
product variant, product.product, item variant, SKU, stockable product, sellable product, finished good, raw material, consumable, internal reference, barcode product, variant combination, product code
Related Models (most joined):

product.template (parent template)
product.attribute.value (variant values)
stock.quant (stock levels)
sale.order.line, purchase.order.line, pos.order.line
mrp.bom, mrp.production
product.pricelist.item
account.account (via category)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
product.product is Odoo’s main variant-level model inheriting from product.template, storing specific SKU (default_code), barcode, attribute combinations, prices, and real-time stock quantities. It is the central record used everywhere for inventory movements, sales/purchase lines, manufacturing, POS, and reporting, representing the actual physical or service item transacted in the system.